--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Components used to build, register or test the engine - NOT redistributed
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Microsoft.CrmSdk.CoreAssemblies - the Dataverse SDK assemblies that
    Ascentix.RulesEngine.Core and .Plugin compile against. Dataverse
    supplies them at runtime; the exported solution's PluginAssemblies folder
    contains only the engine's own AscentixRulesEnginePlugin.dll. Governed
    by the license accompanying that NuGet package.

  esbuild, TypeScript, vitest, jsdom, marked, @playwright/test, the
  @testing-library packages and the @types/* declaration packages (declared in
  client/package.json), and xunit, xunit.runner.visualstudio,
  Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk and FakeXrmEasy.9 (declared in
  tests/Ascentix.RulesEngine.Tests) - each under its own license.

  marked renders this project's own Markdown documentation to HTML during
  `npm run build`; the generated HTML is Ascentix content and no marked code is
  bundled into any web resource.

  tslib is present in client/node_modules as a transitive install but is not
  reachable from any bundle entry point and appears in no shipped web resource.
  (Fluent UI's TypeScript runtime helpers come from @swc/helpers, listed above.)


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Verifying this list
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Run esbuild with `--metafile` over the three `npm run build` entry points
(client/src/index.ts, client/src/authoring/index.ts, client/src/editor/index.tsx);
every third-party input that reaches a shipped bundle is listed in the metafile.
The first two entry points bundle no third-party code at all.
